{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SPbqwu2CvDw7YCVQJcuy5d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# WI-283 — blocked-disposition must regenerate every floor-checked artifact\n2\t\n3\t**WI:** WI-283 · **Status:** queued · **Priority 1** (wedges two lanes of the\n4\tlive 2026-07-23 run) · **Delivers:** the dispatcher's §9 blocked-disposition\n5\ttransaction (no spine SR change; the defect is in `agent_dispatch.py`)\n6\t\n7\t## Problem\n8\t\n9\tLive failure, 2026-07-23, train `3-g3-WI-273-b45e`: the worker blocked\n10\tcorrectly (SR-052 needs a family-heterogeneous CRITIQUE — the WI-243\n11\tfail-closed perceptual gate; §10 puts CRITIQUE in the serial coordinator pass,\n12\tso the worker rightly refused to self-author it). But the coordinator's\n13\t`blocked_disposition()` transaction then **failed its own commit,\n14\tdeterministically, on every retry**:\n15\t\n16\t- Flipping the WI row to `Status=blocked` changes the inputs of the GENERATED\n17\t  \"pending owner-actions\" projection in `docs/open-items.md` (a blocked row is\n18\t  an owner-action).\n19\t- The transaction regenerates the status snapshot (`generate_status`) and the\n20\t  `_regenerate_disposition_artifacts` set — but **not that projection** — so\n21\t  the pre-commit floor's `status-map` step (`gen_trajectory.py --status\n22\t  --check`) refuses the commit: *\"pending owner-actions projection STALE\"*.\n23\t- The train parks `state=error` (journal 07:00:35 + prior), the disposition\n24\t  never lands, and the coordinator **never reaches its SR-084 critique\n25\t  obligation** — the render-critique protocol stalls behind a bookkeeping\n26\t  failure. WI-272 will hit the identical wall when its block records.\n27\t\n28\t## Approach\n29\t\n30\t- In the staging worktree, before the disposition commit, regenerate the SAME\n31\t  artifact set the floor checks — reuse the existing `_regenerate_pending`\n32\t  path (the needs-human branch already calls it) or, better, derive the regen\n33\t  list from one shared home so the transaction and the floor cannot disagree\n34\t  again (the WI-260 \"gate and scheduler read one rule\" precedent, applied to\n35\t  disposition vs floor).\n36\t- Regression test: a fixture train whose blocked WI feeds the pending\n37\t  projection; `blocked_disposition()` must commit clean and the train must\n38\t  reach `blocked` (not `error`).\n39\t- After this lands, the parked `error` trains' dispositions retry and clear on\n40\t  the dispatcher's rescan; verify WI-273 (and WI-272 if blocked by then)\n41\t  transition to `blocked` with their BlockRefs, unblocking the critique\n42\t  dispatch.\n43\t\n44\t## Interfaces\n45\t\n46\tNo cross-module seam — intra-module (`agent_dispatch.py` + its tests).\n47\t\n48\t## Done-when\n49\t\n50\t- [ ] Disposition commits pass the floor when the blocked row feeds any\n51\t      generated projection (test proves the 2026-07-23 shape).\n52\t- [ ] The regen list is single-homed with the floor's checked set (or the\n53\t      divergence risk is explicitly recorded).\n54\t- [ ] Live: `3-g3-WI-273-b45e` reaches `blocked` state on rescan.\n55\t- [ ] Commit bar green; row `done`, spec archived.\n56\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c47a7c9-1a73-4297-bb7c-7af63d0c92ca","uuid":"f8b7a0e1-fd5f-45a4-ad3f-83ee9904ceae","timestamp":"2026-07-24T04:59:02.345Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template-trains\\p0-g3-WI-283-87ef\\docs\\specs\\WI-283.md","content":"# WI-283 — blocked-disposition must regenerate every floor-checked artifact\n\n**WI:** WI-283 · **Status:** queued · **Priority 1** (wedges two lanes of the\nlive 2026-07-23 run) · **Delivers:** the dispatcher's §9 blocked-disposition\ntransaction (no spine SR change; the defect is in `agent_dispatch.py`)\n\n## Problem\n\nLive failure, 2026-07-23, train `3-g3-WI-273-b45e`: the worker blocked\ncorrectly (SR-052 needs a family-heterogeneous CRITIQUE — the WI-243\nfail-closed perceptual gate; §10 puts CRITIQUE in the serial coordinator pass,\nso the worker rightly refused to self-author it). But the coordinator's\n`blocked_disposition()` transaction then **failed its own commit,\ndeterministically, on every retry**:\n\n- Flipping the WI row to `Status=blocked` changes the inputs of the GENERATED\n  \"pending owner-actions\" projection in `docs/open-items.md` (a blocked row is\n  an owner-action).\n- The transaction regenerates the status snapshot (`generate_status`) and the\n  `_regenerate_disposition_artifacts` set — but **not that projection** — so\n  the pre-commit floor's `status-map` step (`gen_trajectory.py --status\n  --check`) refuses the commit: *\"pending owner-actions projection STALE\"*.\n- The train parks `state=error` (journal 07:00:35 + prior), the disposition\n  never lands, and the coordinator **never reaches its SR-084 critique\n  obligation** — the render-critique protocol stalls behind a bookkeeping\n  failure. WI-272 will hit the identical wall when its block records.\n\n## Approach\n\n- In the staging worktree, before the disposition commit, regenerate the SAME\n  artifact set the floor checks — reuse the existing `_regenerate_pending`\n  path (the needs-human branch already calls it) or, better, derive the regen\n  list from one shared home so the transaction and the floor cannot disagree\n  again (the WI-260 \"gate and scheduler read one rule\" precedent, applied to\n  disposition vs floor).\n- Regression test: a fixture train whose blocked WI feeds the pending\n  projection; `blocked_disposition()` must commit clean and the train must\n  reach `blocked` (not `error`).\n- After this lands, the parked `error` trains' dispositions retry and clear on\n  the dispatcher's rescan; verify WI-273 (and WI-272 if blocked by then)\n  transition to `blocked` with their BlockRefs, unblocking the critique\n  dispatch.\n\n## Interfaces\n\nNo cross-module seam — intra-module (`agent_dispatch.py` + its tests).\n\n## Done-when\n\n- [ ] Disposition commits pass the floor when the blocked row feeds any\n      generated projection (test proves the 2026-07-23 shape).\n- [ ] The regen list is single-homed with the floor's checked set (or the\n      divergence risk is explicitly recorded).\n- [ ] Live: `3-g3-WI-273-b45e` reaches `blocked` state on rescan.\n- [ ] Commit bar green; row `done`, spec archived.\n","numLines":56,"startLine":1,"totalLines":56}}}
