{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VB18hz22mXKTF6MLdBmdt2","type":"tool_result","content":"1190\tdef _regenerate_disposition_artifacts(worktree):\n1191\t    \"\"\"Regenerate freshness-gated views after a disposition edits registries.\n1192\t\n1193\t    The generators are kit-owned siblings of this dispatcher even when the\n1194\t    checkout is a downstream scaffold. Artifact presence is the opt-in signal:\n1195\t    a non-adopter must not depend on either generator.\n1196\t    \"\"\"\n1197\t    worktree = Path(worktree)\n1198\t    scripts = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n1199\t    generators = []\n1200\t    if (worktree / \"docs\" / \"okf\").is_dir():\n1201\t        generators.append((\"gen_okf.py\", []))\n1202\t    if (worktree / \"PROJECT_STATE.html\").is_file():\n1203\t        generators.append((\"gen_trajectory.py\", []))\n1204\t    # WI-284/WI-283: the status.md snapshot (derived gate/spine + open-items +\n1205\t    # the generated Ready-frontier list) and the open-items.md pending\n1206\t    # projection are freshness-gated by the `status-map` step, but a disposition\n1207\t    # that flips a WI to done/blocked changes their inputs. Regenerate them here\n1208\t    # so the disposition commit passes its own floor (WI-283) AND the just-closed\n1209\t    # id drops out of the generated frontier automatically (WI-284 — no stranded\n1210\t    # done-id to redden a later train's DONE gate). Opt-in on the marker, like\n1211\t    # the two generators above: a status.md/open-items.md without the generated\n1212\t    # blocks is left untouched, so a non-adopter regenerates nothing.\n1213\t    if (worktree / \"docs\" / \"status.md\").is_file():\n1214\t        generators.append((\"gen_trajectory.py\", [\"--status\"]))\n1215\t    for name, extra in generators:\n1216\t        proc = subprocess.run(\n1217\t            [sys.executable, str(scripts / name), \"--root\", str(worktree), *extra],\n1218\t            cwd=str(worktree),\n1219\t            capture_output=True,\n1220\t            text=True,\n1221\t            encoding=\"utf-8\",\n1222\t            errors=\"replace\",\n1223\t            stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL,\n1224\t        )\n1225\t        if proc.returncode != 0:\n1226\t            tail = ((proc.stdout or \"\") + (proc.stderr or \"\")).strip()[-400:]\n1227\t            return False, \"disposition regen failed ({}): {}\".format(\n1228\t                name, tail or \"exit {}\".format(proc.returncode)\n1229\t            )\n1230\t    return True, \"\"\n1231\t\n1232\t\n1233\tdef _salvage_round_evidence(root, worktree, tid, old_head=None):\n1234\t    \"\"\"Best-effort copy of DP-* evidence before a hard reset: uncommitted\n1235\t    changes via porcelain (the only scan that sees untracked files) plus,\n1236\t    when the reset target is known, tracked changes already committed past\n1237\t    it — those files are still on disk because salvage runs pre-reset. Both\n1238\t    scans use NUL-delimited output so Git never C-quotes non-ASCII/special\n1239\t    path bytes; malformed records simply contribute no round name.\"\"\"\n1240\t    round_names = set()\n1241\t\n1242\t    def note(rel):\n1243\t     
