{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdLLK9qXmkLCtpWqsTHC7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The full pre-commit floor is green (all 8 steps, exit 0), and the directly-affected test modules already passed (151 + 64 tests). I'm now waiting on the full unfiltered suite (the WI-close bar) which is running in the background — `pytest -q -n auto` buffers output until the end, so I'll get the result when it finishes.\n\nHere's where things stand:\n\n**Implemented (WI-283):**\n- `agent_dispatch.py`: introduced `_STATUS_MAP_MARKERS` + `_DISPOSITION_REGEN` as the **single home** for the disposition regen family, and refactored `_regenerate_disposition_artifacts` to iterate it. The `status-map` opt-in now matches the floor's gate exactly (`status.md` **OR** `open-items.md`) instead of `status.md` alone.\n- `test_agent_dispatch_decisions.py`: binding tests pinning each regen entry's generator+flags to the floor's `check.steps()` command, a tripwire on the pre-commit floor's step list, and the opt-in-marker assertion.\n- `test_agent_loop_integrate.py`: end-to-end regression proving the 2026-07-23 shape (a blocked WI feeding the pending projection → `blocked_disposition` reaches `integrated` and the composed tree passes `gen_trajectory.py --status --check`), plus a discriminating unit test that fails on the pre-fix opt-in.\n\n**Key finding I verified honestly:** `generate_status()` synthesizes `docs/status.md` before every disposition regen, so the old `status.md`-only opt-in tracked the floor only *incidentally* — it masked the mismatch end-to-end but left the regen wrong on its own terms. The single-home makes it correct independent of that side-effect. Comments in code and tests state this accurately rather than overclaiming a reachable end-to-end failure.\n\nI'll commit with the WI trailers once the full suite reports green."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tok